{% block demo_examples %}
## Examples

The examples run on the bundled synthetic experiment, `load_ab_test()`, with its
assignment table, `load_ab_test_assignment()`, as `assignment`.

### Scorecard

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.ab_test(
    ("exp_group", "treatment", "control"),
    metrics=[
        {"name": "conversion", "metric": "has_event", "metric_args": {"event": "order_success"}},
        {"name": "adders", "metric": "has_any_event", "metric_args": {"events": ["add_to_cart", "quick_add"]}},
        {"name": "orders_per_user", "metric": "event_count", "metric_args": {"event": "order_success"}},
        {"name": "revenue_per_user", "metric": "column_sum", "metric_args": {"column": "order_value"}},
        {"name": "aov", "metric": "column_sum", "metric_args": {"column": "order_value"},
         "denominator": {"metric": "event_count", "metric_args": {"event": "order_success"}}},
    ],
    assignment=assignment,
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/ab-test/scorecard.html" height={620} />

Every row is grey: the top line is inconclusive. Read conversion's interval, not
its dot: effects from about −1 pp to about +2.3 pp remain possible.

### Strata and periods

`platform` is fixed at signup, so it is declared pre-exposure. The weekly rows
drift from positive in the first weeks to below zero later. Calendar weeks mix
users of every exposure age, so this does not measure how the effect changes
with exposure; the
[A/B Testing guide](/docs/ab-testing#periods-horizon-and-novelty) does that by
time since assignment.

<DemoWidget cmd={`stream.ab_test(
    ("exp_group", "treatment", "control"),
    metrics=[
        {"name": "conversion", "metric": "has_event", "metric_args": {"event": "order_success"}},
        {"name": "revenue_per_user", "metric": "column_sum", "metric_args": {"column": "order_value"}},
    ],
    assignment=assignment,
    strata_col="platform",
    strata_pre_exposure=True,
    period="W",
)`} path="/docs-demos/widgets/ab-test/strata-periods.html" height={720} />
